<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB6-026>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB6-026" ;
  triage:title "run_bb6_prompt_handoffs.py scenario_disabled_reminder uses a fixed sleep instead of a bounded poll to prove a disabled reminder never fires" ;
  triage:description "flaky-test-qa (2026-09-13T04:33:21Z), found during BB-POST-MORTEM-1789304000 phase-ending gate on integrate/phase-bb. scripts/smoke/run_bb6_prompt_handoffs.py:384 scenario_disabled_reminder uses a fixed time.sleep(REMINDER_WAIT_SECONDS) (65.0s, line 26) to prove a disabled task_reminder never fires. Production reminder cadence is TASK_REMINDER_INTERVAL_MS = 60_000 (crates/atm-storage/src/task_store.rs:32) -- only ~5s/8% margin, and that margin only starts after real wall-clock time already spent on assign()+wait_for_pane('ready') inside a live colima container. This is a fixed-sleep standing in for real synchronization (no-flaky-test-tolerance standard): can false-pass if daemon cadence shifts, or false-fail/flake if colima/docker latency shifts. Not a regression of BB6-024 (reader_pool.rs harness race, separately re-confirmed fixed by the same reviewer in this same gate) -- a distinct, newly-discovered gap in the BB6.7 colima smoke script." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-quality" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "flaky-test-qa via quality-mgr, BB-POST-MORTEM-1789304000 phase-ending gate" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "scripts/smoke/run_bb6_prompt_handoffs.py (scenario_disabled_reminder, line 384; REMINDER_WAIT_SECONDS, line 26; existing wait_for_pane/deadline poll pattern at line 117)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-13T04:33:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (2026-09-13, team-lead): important, not blocking -- Phase BB stack is already fully landed (all 19 PRs merged into integrate/phase-bb); this is a smoke-script test-hardening gap, not a production defect or an observed flake. Does not block the integrate/phase-bb -> develop merge. Filed as fast-follow: replace the fixed sleep with a bounded poll mirroring the wait_for_pane/deadline pattern already used at line 117 -- any reminder=\"...\" block appearing for the task is an immediate hard failure; deadline elapsing (derived from TASK_REMINDER_INTERVAL_MS + an explicit multiplier, not a bare literal) is the pass condition. Land in the same fast-follow branch as BB6-028 (prompt_handoff_record.rs log_failure() missing outcome= field) -- same colima/prompt-handoff observability surface." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-13T04:33:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB6-026/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

